# Auth Forms & Errors

## Validation

- Validate email/password (and other fields) on the server before `signUp` / `signInWithPassword` / similar.
- Reject empty, malformed, or out-of-policy inputs early; do not call Supabase with invalid data.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
await supabase.auth.signInWithPassword({ email, password })

// ✅ GOOD
const parsed = loginSchema.safeParse({ email, password })
if (!parsed.success) return { error: "Invalid email or password." }
await supabase.auth.signInWithPassword(parsed.data)
```

## Errors shown to users

- Never return raw Supabase/Postgres messages or stack traces to the UI.
- Use generic copy (e.g. "Invalid email or password.", "Unable to create account.").
- Log full error details only on the server.

## Components

- Forms that need state/handlers: Client Components.
- Data fetching and session reads for protected pages: Server Components by default.
